        "en": "International organisations such as UNESCO have designated hundreds of locations as World Heritage Sites, conferring recognition upon places deemed to possess outstanding universal value. This designation frequently attracts tourism revenue that can fund restoration and conservation projects. Yet the relationship between tourism and preservation is inherently ambivalent. Excessive visitor numbers exert physical pressure upon fragile structures, while the commercialisation of sacred rituals for tourist consumption may dilute their authentic cultural significance.",
        "zh": "联合国教科文组织等国际机构已将数百处地点列为世界遗产，对被认为具有突出普遍价值的场所予以认可。这一认定常常吸引旅游收入，为修复与保护项目提供资金。然而，旅游与保护之间的关系本身充满矛盾。过量游客对脆弱结构造成物理压力，而将神圣仪式商业化以供游客消费，则可能稀释其真实的文化意义。"
